# Response headers for static assets.
#
# Only public marketing pages are affected. /api/*, /s/*, /e/*, /p/* and
# /via/* are listed in run_worker_first in wrangler.jsonc, so they never
# reach the assets layer and never see these rules — their headers come
# from html()/json() in src/lib.js instead.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent discovery, on every public page.
#
# RFC 8288 links to the machine-readable descriptions of this site.
# All four targets are one comma-separated Link header, which RFC 8288
# Section 3.5 defines as exactly equivalent to four separate headers —
# fewer moving parts, and no reliance on how _headers merges repeats.
#
# Relation types are all IANA-registered, so they are legal as bare
# lowercase tokens: api-catalog (RFC 9727), service-desc and service-doc
# (RFC 8631), describedby (W3C POWDER).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
/*
  Link: </.well-known/api-catalog>; rel="api-catalog"; type="application/linkset+json", </openapi.json>; rel="service-desc"; type="application/json", </api-docs/>; rel="service-doc"; type="text/html", </llms.txt>; rel="describedby"; type="text/plain"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The API catalog itself.
#
# RFC 9727 Section 6.2 makes application/linkset+json mandatory at this
# location, and Section 4.2 asks for the profile parameter. The file has
# no extension, so without this rule the assets layer would guess.
#
# RFC 9727 Section 2 also requires a HEAD of this URL to come back
# carrying an api-catalog Link header — checkers test HEAD, not just GET.
# The /* rule above already supplies one and the two rules merge, so
# there is deliberately no Link line repeated here.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
/.well-known/api-catalog
  Content-Type: application/linkset+json; profile="https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9727"
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# Markdown documents are served as markdown, not as a download.
/auth.md
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8

/llms.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
